orty nine video screens at the same  time zoom is perfect for you it also  gives you the ability to teleconference  in a total of 1,000 people on their  premium enterprise paid package the free  version of zoom actually only allows you  a hundred people in the teleconference  which is actually a pretty huge number  for a free platform if you're looking to  run webinars training sessions classroom  education style videos or anything of  those sorts sue is the perfect platform  here it allows virtual hand raising of  all your participants so you can easily  find out who needs to say something and  when it also gives you a whole bunch of  analytical data afterwards that you can  review if you want to another great  feature here is it has interactive polls  and questions and answers so if you're  hosting a webinar for example or a class  you can easily post the Q&amp;A and get a  whole bunch of feedback very quickly and  very effectively to move forward with  that webinars if you want to keep a  record of the teleconference or  videoconference you can easily record  and save straight to your hard drive or  to the cloud if you want to you can also  share your screen directly with  individuals if you need them to see  something on your screen one of the  downsides of zoom is you can only host a  40-minute videoconference with the free  version you can host up to 24 hours if  you're willing to pay 20 dollars 99  cents Australian per month for the  professional version one thing I almost  forgot with zoom is the simple fact that  if you're an e-commerce entrepreneur and  you want to start selling some classes  or some webinars or some sort of  information on a regular basis you can  set up a registration fee with zoom so  you can invite a whole bunch of people  to come and watch this webinar or  seminar that you're hosting and for  example charge them a five dollar  registration fee so all of a sudden  you've made a business out of zoom  moving onto skype now  is very similar to the zoom platform  however unlike zoo you can't access it  anywhere without an account if you want  to use Skype you do need the app  installed or a user somehow in some way  shape or form this limits you to being  somewhat technologically savvy to be  able to create a Skype account and set  something out and then invite somebody  into a chat it is a little bit of a  complex process and it isn't as easy as  oome so that's definitely a draw down  for Skype you can have up to 50 people  on a teleconference or a videoconference  on skype which is a little bit less than  zoom but it doesn't give you the same  abilities of recording your screen  sharing your screen questions and  answers and a couple polls here and  there one of the other benefits of Skype  is privacy along with having encrypted  conversations which all of them have its  standard it also gives you the ability  to blur out the background so if you're  sitting at home with your kids running  around in the background or if your  environment is a little bit less  professional than you'd like it to be  you can easily blur out the background  to make sure nobody sees what's going on  and I think the best feature that Skype  has is a real-time live translator so if  I was here speaking to you in a  completely different language you could  have a little text line at the bottom of  your screen directly translating into  you in real-time so if you for example  had a cousin in Germany that you wanted  to wish a happy birthday you could use  Skype to communicate with them very  effectively and very quickly Scott does  also have Skype business which is now  called Microsoft teams but I'm not gonna  dive into that too much because it isn't  cross-compatible across all platforms  and you really want to be able to use  something it doesn't matter who you're  talking to if there are an iPhone and  Android a old smartphone a tablet  whatever and you want to be able to use  that software  moving on to WebEx and if you haven't  heard of WebEx before that's okay  because women is targeted at your  premium enterprises with millions of  dollars to spend on this sort of stuff  but that doesn't mean  everybody can't use it so WebEx can host  up to a hundred thousand people on the  same teleconference at any given time  that's more people than I know in this  world and probably more people that  actually met throughout my whole  lifetime face-to-face and had a  conversation with that hundred thousand  people is limited to twenty five videos  on its screen which is again more than  enough for those people just like zoom  WebEx is able to run a whole bunch of  different platforms you can record your  screen share your screen questions and  answers' polls ecommerce related  webinars and seminars where you charge  people to watch your content and  basically everything that zoom can do  where WebEx goes over and above is a  simple fact  again it is targeted at these larger  enterprises that have millions of  dollars to spend so it hosts its own  products and platforms that you can  purchase later on down the track if you  want so if you wanted a whiteboard  dedicated to drawing and sharing alive  during a webinar then you can buy a  WebEx whiteboard and share that directly  it's a physical whiteboard it's  something tangible that you can use  during these seminars they also produce  their own at video screens video cameras  and microphones to make your meeting  rooms that little bit more special and a  little bit more professional  so to recap I think zoom is probably the  best for all users who are just looking  to start a video conference Skype is  probably more your medium-sized business  that wants to limit it to individuals  within their company and just use it as  a platform to chat basically you can do  it absolutely everything you can do on  skype and that you can do on zoo so if  you already set up on skype just that on  skype there isn't too many added  benefits in zoo for anybody up to a  hundred participants in that  conversation and finally WebEx I think  is for the top dogs out there the guys  that have millions of dollars to throw  at this and it really invests heavily  into it if this is something you're  doing on a regular basis and it isn't  just because of the code of 19 per  Demick then I think WebEx is something  to actually look into and invest your  money into that's all from me today guys  I hope you enjoyed this special edition  that brought on by the kerbin 19  pandemic if you did and want more tech  reviews of all sorts of different tech  products from mobile phones to laptops  to everything in between make sure you  smash that subscribe button  20:20 style and as always I'll see you  next Monday

